        "sources": {
            "supplies.plus": "the battery block below",
            "battery": "per cell, a typical LiCoO2 LiPo (estimate: no datasheet for a generic 2S RC pack). Rest voltages 100..5 %: 4.20, 4.11, 4.02, 3.95, 3.87, 3.84, 3.80, 3.77, 3.73, 3.69, 3.61 V (voltagebasics.com 'Lithium polymer battery voltage chart'); 0 % = the rated cut-off, 3.0 V at the terminals at 0.2 C (cell datasheet convention), so 3.05 V here (the ~3.27 V such charts give for 0 % is after the cell has rested, a relaxation this model leaves out); below 0 %: the knee to ~2.5 V within ~1.5 % more charge (estimate). Resistance ~15 mOhm per cell for a small 20C pack, rising near empty (estimate). Over-discharge: below 3.0 V per cell a LiPo is damaged (common RC practice; a warning, no damage model)",
            "battery.rate": "fitted with tools/fit_battery.py (the simulation's own model) to typical LiPo rate capability (estimate, the shape of cell datasheets' rate charts): 100 % at 0.2 C, 97 % at 1 C, 95 % at 2 C, to 3.0 V; rms error 0.4 %. Time constant ~45 s: also gives a little of the voltage recovery after a load stops",
            "battery.protection": "a DW01A-class protection IC (the common one on Li-ion protection boards): over-discharge detection 2.40 V (2.30-2.50) per cell, delay 40 ms typical (40-100 ms), release 3.0 V only with a charger connected (DW01A datasheets). An RC LiPo pack has none fitted by default: the Inspector's 'Protection circuit (BMS)' adds one"
        }
    },
